# What never reaches a Docker build context.
#
# The api image is built from the repository root (`.github/workflows/build.yml` passes
# `context: .`), so this file is the first fence of the image's supply chain: anything
# listed here cannot be copied into a layer by a `COPY` that is wider than its author
# meant, and cannot be read by a build step at all. `apps/worker/` has its own, because
# the worker image is built from its own directory.
#
# Three kinds of entry:
#   - secrets and local state, which must never be in an image (`[SEC1]`);
#   - the host's build products, so a stale `dist/` or `node_modules/` on a laptop can
#     never become the thing that ships — the image builds its own;
#   - everything the runtime does not need, which is most of the repository.
#
# `contracts/` is here for a reason ADR 0031 states: it is a top-level fixture directory,
# read by both tiers' test suites and imported by nothing. Excluding it from the context
# makes "no `contracts/` in the image" structural rather than a promise.

# Secrets and local state
.env
.env.*
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.cubic
.ordna
.scratch

# The host's build products — the image builds its own
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.vite
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
**/reports
**/.stryker-tmp
*.log

# Not runtime, not build input
.github
apps/docs-site
apps/worker
contracts
deploy
docs
cubic.yaml
renovate.json
